		ctx = templ.ClearChildren(ctx)
		templ_7745c5c3_Err = templruntime.WriteString(templ_7745c5c3_Buffer, 8, "<section id=\"nature-purpose\"><h2>5. Nature and purpose of processing</h2><p>Kiff Agents OÜ Processes Audit Data only as necessary to provide the Service: receiving proposals and tool calls, evaluating them against the Controller's configuration and Cards, holding them for human approval where the configuration so requires, forwarding an authorized call to the connected tool or issuing an authorization the tool verifies, recording the decisions and the outcome the tool reports, emitting signed Receipts, and (where the Controller has so configured) publishing tamper-evident summary hashes to a public verifiable trail. The connected tool performs the underlying action; an authorization decision alone is not evidence that the action was performed.</p><p>For tafs, Kiff Agents OÜ also Processes tafs Data to run each taf the Controller starts: running it on its schedule and in chats with the Controller's people, sending its tool calls through KIFF, keeping its runs, chats and memory notes so it can report and continue its work, and alerting the Controller's registered devices when a call is held. Through Setup and planque it also connects the Controller's tools when the Controller's people sign in at the tool's provider and approve the connection on their device: for an app planque signs in to itself, such as Stripe, or a key the Controller gives, planque keeps that token or key, encrypted, and uses it only to make a call KIFF has decided; for a managed connection, Composio holds the sign-in and makes only the calls planque asks for, and planque keeps the connection's record and the tools approved. KIFF uses managed connections only for the apps named on <a href=\"/subprocessors#composio\">kiff.dev/subprocessors</a>. Annex 4 sets out the data, where it is kept and for how long.</p></section>")
